{% extends '@CitadelAureum/core/docs/layout.html.twig' %}

{% block article %}
    <p>
        Streetle is a training game for front-of-house teams. It shows the
        streets around the hotel with every name hidden. Click a street, type
        its name, and see how well you really know the area guests ask about.
    </p>

    <p>
        When the hotel's location is set, the hotel is marked on the map so
        you can work outwards from the front door.
    </p>
    <p>
        The map is shaded with Manchester's neighbourhoods, using the same
        names and colours as the Visit Manchester city map handed to guests,
        so you learn which streets belong to Ancoats, Spinningfields, the
        Northern Quarter and the rest.
    </p>
    <p>
        Parks, museums, Manchester Art Gallery, the Arndale and Afflecks are
        marked to help you find your bearings, and tram stops show as yellow
        symbols. Zoom in to see their names. Tram stops stay unnamed because
        many are named after the street they sit on.
    </p>

    <h2>Game modes</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Sprint</strong> gives you five minutes to name as many streets as you can. <strong>Skip</strong> moves past a street you don't know.</li>
        <li><strong>Free play</strong> has no clock. Work through the map at your own pace and press <strong>End session</strong> when you're done.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Common tasks</h2>
    <ol class="au-docs-steps">
        <li>Pick a mode on the Streetle page and press <strong>Start</strong>.</li>
        <li>Click a street. It turns orange. Type its name and press <strong>Guess</strong>. Abbreviations such as <em>St</em>, <em>Rd</em> and <em>Sq</em> are accepted.</li>
        <li>If you name a different street, Streetle tells you how far away it is.</li>
        <li><strong>Hint</strong> shows the shape of the name, then one more letter of each word, up to three times.</li>
        <li>When the session ends you see your streets named, time, streets per minute and accuracy, plus where you rank and who is just ahead of you.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Your recent games</h2>
    <p>
        The Streetle page lists your last ten games of either mode, with the
        streets you named, your time and accuracy, and a link back to each
        set of results.
    </p>

    <h2>The leaderboard</h2>
    <p>
        Each mode has its own leaderboard showing everyone's best session.
        Sprint is ranked by streets named, then accuracy. Free play is ranked
        by streets named, then the fastest time.
    </p>

    <div class="au-docs-note">
        <i class="ph ph-info"></i>
        <p>
            Managers download the map once with <strong>Download map</strong>,
            and can refresh it later to pick up new streets. Map data comes
            from OpenStreetMap.
        </p>
    </div>
{% endblock %}
